WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
The refrigeration cycle is the foundation of everything you'll do in this trade.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
The pressure-temperature relationship is the foundation of refrigerant
diagnostics. Every refrigerant has a specific saturation temperature at each
pressure. For R-410A at 118 psig the saturation temp is about 40F. You use the

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
PT Chart: Shows saturation temperature for each refrigerant at every pressure.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
R-410A: Standard residential AC refrigerant operating at higher pressures than
R-22.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: You will calculate superheat and subcooling
on every cooling diagnostic call.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Use the PT chart for the CORRECT refrigerant. And —
Superheat measured at suction line, subcooling at liquid line

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Before you move on — what happens to refrigerant in the evaporator? Don't look
it up. Think about it.

